  "notes": {
    "raw": "\\*Enthalpy of formation and entropy at 298 K estimated. \nHeat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations: \n<table><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">298.15-1800 K:</td><td> $Cp^o$  = 15.887 + 3.740x $10^{-3}$ T - 0.704x $10^5$ T $^{-2}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $H^o$ - $H_{298}^o$  = 15.887x $10^{-3}$ T + 1.870x $10^{-6}$ T $^2$  + 0.704x $10^2$ T $^{-1}$  - 5.139</td></tr></table>\nReaction equations (kcal/mol): \n<table><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">298.15-1800 K:</td><td> $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = -171.351 + 1.935 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} + 0.640 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} + 2.100 \\text{T}^{-1}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -171.351 - 1.935 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} \\ln \\text{T} - 0.640 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} + 1.050 \\text{T}^{-1} + 58.269 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T}$ </td></tr></table>\nSources: Enthalpy of formation and entropy at 298 K are those estimated by Mills (80). Other data based on Volovik (125). ",
